## Detection Queries

### Detect Failed Logins

```spl
index=lab_logs EventID=4625

Detect Brute Force (Repeated Attempts)

index=lab_logs EventID=4625
| stats count min(_time) as firstSeen max(_time) as lastSeen by Account_Name SourceIp
| eval duration = lastSeen - firstSeen
| where count >= 5 AND duration <= 300

Detect Multiple Accounts Targeted (Password Spraying)

index=lab_logs EventID=4625
| stats dc(Account_Name) as unique_accounts by SourceIp
| where unique_accounts > 3

Analysis

Multiple failed login attempts were observed against the admin account.
All attempts originated from the same IP address 192.168.1.100.
The login failures occurred within a short time window.
Pattern Observed:
Same account
Same source IP
Rapid repeated attempts
Conclusion:
This behavior is consistent with a brute force attack, where an attacker is attempting to guess the password of a specific account.
Additional Insight:
If multiple accounts were targeted instead, this would indicate password spraying.

What Was Done

Source IP 192.168.1.100 was blocked
Targeted account (admin) was locked and password reset
Incident escalated for further investigation
Additional monitoring enabled for authentication activity


